{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fa9df87e-4473-4b59-9a8a-3f7517eb95d2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Claude-Opus-4.8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JQFwnW1WwArgYE5bcSuj2F","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L1-092_gqa_attention_with_qk_norm/candidates.jsonl","old_string":"\"next\": \"c002: shape-specialized tiling/autotune for projection + output GEMMs (largest FLOP share).\"}","new_string":"\"next\": \"c002: shape-specialized tiling/autotune for projection + output GEMMs (largest FLOP share).\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_sha256\": \"b6397e02f969cfe32e3cbf9754f7d544945299d2be3e315ebcea176adabe164f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T00:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"H2: the projection + output GEMMs are the FLOP bottleneck (~650 GFLOP vs ~55 attention); replacing the fixed 64x64x32 unswizzled GEMM with an autotuned, L2-swizzled (GROUP_M) matmul using fp32 tl.dot(a,b,acc) and an EVEN_K fast path recovers cuBLAS-competitive throughput and lifts geomean.\", \"design_delta\": \"Single delta vs c001: _gemm_kernel replaced by @triton.autotune (8 configs over BLOCK_M/N/K, GROUP_M=8, num_warps/stages) with grid-swizzle, modulo-wrapped A/B row/col loads, EVEN_K branch (K=4096 and K=12288 both divisible by 64 -> no inner K mask), masked store. RMSNorm+RoPE kernel and flash-attention kernel byte-identical to c001.\", \"static_validation\": {\"math_checklist\": \"pass\", \"structural_checklist\": \"pass\", \"notes\": \"GEMM math identical (C=A@Bw^T+bias, fp32 accum, bf16 store); EVEN_K path safe since both K values %64==0; modulo wrap on M/N loads harmless because store is masked to M,N; grep confirms no Torch compute op in path (only comments/docstring mention linear).\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"ccea3f00\", \"B\": 1, \"S\": 128, \"correct\": true, \"ref_ms\": 0.869507, \"cand_ms\": 0.3404115, \"speedup\": 2.5543}, {\"uuid\": \"1e96cc88\", \"B\": 4, \"S\": 293, \"correct\": true, \"ref_ms\": 3.533792, \"cand_ms\": 1.6318985, \"speedup\": 2.1654}, {\"uuid\": \"d0ce8c45\", \"B\": 1, \"S\": 1024, \"correct\": true, \"ref_ms\": 4.3817165, \"cand_ms\": 1.642171, \"speedup\": 2.6682}, {\"uuid\": \"c92bb0a5\", \"B\": 1, \"S\": 512, \"correct\": true, \"ref_ms\": 1.686089, \"cand_ms\": 0.8424055, \"speedup\": 2.0015}, {\"uuid\": \"65a1864d\", \"B\": 8, \"S\": 373, \"correct\": true, \"ref_ms\": 9.11431, \"cand_ms\": 3.913409, \"speedup\": 2.3290}], \"all_correct\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 2.3308, \"average_speedup\": 2.3437, \"decision\": \"keep\", \"reason\": \"PASS 5/5, geomean 2.3308x vs c001 1.7135x (+36%). H2 confirmed: tuned GEMMs are the dominant lever. Biggest jumps on small-M (S=128: 1.46->2.55) and largest-M (B8 S373: 1.60->2.33) cases where c001's untuned GEMM capped throughput. New frontier = c002. Attention kernel now the next-largest remaining share.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 2, \"skills_used\": [], \"skills_note\": \"KernelWiki (Blackwell/Hopper tcgen05/TMEM) out-of-scope for Ampere sm_80; no-profiler rule bars ncu.\", \"next\": \"c003: flash-attention tiling delta (BLOCK_M/BLOCK_N + num_warps/stages autotune) on top of c002 GEMMs; then consider norm+RoPE fusion / KV-load reuse.\"}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50989,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8df798b-a9b9-45b8-9fc1-9cba86dca820","uuid":"d4eaed18-f2e9-41e6-88e5-f91bfca01277","timestamp":"2026-09-16T18:00:08.135Z"}
